{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "medicine-2026",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-55",
  "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B007",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries defining the distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages of adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B030",
    "B004"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B007 identifies the complementary cellular lineages that organize adaptive immunity, a fundamental framework whose breadth and medical relevance have endured across infection, autoimmunity, cancer, and transplantation. The proposed two-person configuration remains unusually concise and intelligible for the paired lineage discoveries. B030 has a uniquely direct and durable preventive consequence, but that comparative strength does not displace the exceptional conceptual reach and focused attribution of B007.",
    "case_against": "The historical development of lymphocyte biology involved important contributors beyond Miller and Cooper. A citation must therefore remain narrowly directed to the defining distinction of B- and T-lymphocyte lineages rather than imply credit for all subsequent work on lymphocyte development, function, or adaptive immunity.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson favors B030 because it combines a defined VLP vaccine principle with mature prevention of HPV infection and related cancers, while recognizing the need to delimit foundational work from later development and implementation.",
        "response": "I agree that B030's sustained cancer-prevention benefit is extraordinary and that a narrowly framed VLP citation is essential. The remaining issue is whether the three proposed names cleanly capture the decisive scientific and translational steps without absorbing major later contributions. By comparison, B007 can be confined more directly to complementary lineage discoveries by two scientists, while retaining fundamental biological scope."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg argues that B030's clear biological principle and exceptionally consequential preventive outcome give it priority over foundational alternatives, subject to careful attribution.",
        "response": "The direct preventive outcome is a powerful reason to regard B030 as my leading alternative. I give B007 a narrow edge because the discovery of distinct B- and T-cell lineages is itself a durable organizing principle for the entire adaptive immune system, and its proposed attribution requires fewer judgments across the long path from experimental discovery to clinical deployment."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
        "point": "Svenningsson emphasizes that B030 has a coherent discovery-to-prevention linkage but notes that the proposed trio must be separated from clinical, industrial, implementation, and public-health contributions.",
        "response": "I share that caution and regard it as material rather than merely editorial. B030 remains highly meritorious even with a disciplined boundary, but B007 presently offers the more compact configuration for a discovery of comparable maturity and wider foundational reach. B004 likewise remains a strong alternative because of its focused two-person attribution."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record permits a citation centered on Miller and Cooper that is sufficiently bounded without underrepresenting other contributors to lymphocyte-lineage biology.",
      "Whether further historical assessment would establish that Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller are as cleanly bounded for the VLP vaccine achievement as the Miller-Cooper configuration is for B007."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "The supplied profile documents coauthorship with committee colleague Thomas Perlmann, but no candidate-specific connection to the preferred B007 laureates or the listed alternatives is apparent."
  }
}
